# Context
We are currently in a Development Environment.

# General Guidelines
- Do NOT run production builds (like `npm run build`) unless explicitly asked by the me.
- Do NOT apply quick optimizations to "fix" build warnings (like renaming Vike Envs to `PUBLIC_ENV__BASE_URL`) if it risks breaking the `npm run dev` environment.
- Always prioritize functionality within the `npm run dev` server.

# API Guidelines
- Prefix every new backend API call with `API_URL` (imported from `@/lib/flairapi`), never a bare `/businesses/...` path and never a hardcoded host string. Use `flairapi` from `lib/flairapi` to make the requests.
- `API_URL` reads `import.meta.env.VITE_API_URL`, which Vite inlines at build time. Do NOT use `import.meta.env.BASE_URL` — that's Vite's own reserved deploy-base-path constant (default `"/"`), unrelated to this project's API host. This codebase used to hardcode the literal `'https://api.flairsync.com/api/v1'` in every service file to work around that mistake; that's gone now — every environment (dev/staging/prod) sets its own `VITE_API_URL` build arg instead (see Dockerfile.prod). Don't reintroduce the hardcoded literal.
